# tio_a_sets.rules — stage A: set functions (TR292F) in the specification form `?s set:fn ( args )` (TR292C §2).
#
# ── Pools are helper facts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   ?r tmf:memberOf ?c                # ?r is a member of container ?c: its input rdfs:member, plus whatever its set
#                                     # functions define (TR292F §3, §4). Several set functions on one node are a
#                                     # union (TR292A; DEVIATIONS.md entry 1). Never written as rdfs:member, so a pool
#                                     # never reaches the result contract (ContractExtractor copies rdfs:member only
#                                     # for tmf:chosenFor members); 1,000 free ports stay helper facts.
#   ?n tmf:proxyOf "literal"          # a literal member (set:valuesOfObjectProperty values, a literal rdfs:member) is
#                                     # represented by the node ?n = makeSkolem(tmf:LiteralMember, literal): the same
#                                     # literal always gives the same node, so membership tests compare as usual.
#   ?c tmf:container tmf:Yes          # ?c is read as a container: a subject of a set function, an argument container
#                                     # of a set function, an icm:chooseFrom pool or a log:match* container. Only
#                                     # these get their rdfs:member lifted to tmf:memberOf.
# Why the member is the subject: before adding a derived triple Jena's RETE engine checks that it is new with
# find(s, p, o), which scans every triple of the subject. With the pool as subject a 1,000-member pool costs about
# 500,000 comparisons per pool (measured: ~300 ms for the seed with 1,000 free UNI ports); with the member as subject
# each check reads only that resource's few triples. A literal cannot be a subject, hence the proxy nodes.
#
# ── Set constructors are not boolean contributors (tio_a_core: tmf:producesSet) ────────────────────────────────
# set:resourcesOfType, resourcesWithProperty, resourcesWithPropertyObject, valuesOfObjectProperty, union,
# intersection and difference have a container as result (fun:resultType rdfs:Container). They produce tmf:memberOf
# only: no contribution node, no tmf:hasContributor (tio_a_core skips them even when the ontology declares them
# fun:Function), so (a) they never give an element a boolean (an element whose only function is a set constructor
# has no contributor and gets the default false, TR292E §4), and (b) a pool node, typed or anonymous, has no
# contribution that could stay without value. Unimplemented set constructors (typesOfMembers, members*, newest/
# oldestMember) stay off the implemented list and fail closed in tio_a_core (a false contribution on their subject).
#
# ── Boolean set functions are contributors (TR292F §5) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# set:isMember, elementOf, empty, includedIn, intersectsWith, identical (§5 text; not in the vocabulary appendix) and
# forAll get a contribution node exactly like the quantity functions (same skolem as tio_a_core):
#   ?s tmf:contribution ?k . ?k tmf:function set:isMember ; tmf:arguments ?list ; rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate .
# Their value needs negation over membership ("x is not a member"), so it is written in stage B
# (tio_b_sets.rules) from the membership facts derived here, which are complete when stage B starts. Decided here
# (tmf:valuedInA, rdf:value false, tmf:failure): an argument object that is not a list or too few arguments
# ("missing operand nodes"), and a container argument whose membership is not final (below). Positive facts for
# stage B: `?k tmf:setHit tmf:Yes` (isMember: x is in some container; elementOf: x is in all; empty: some container
# has a member; intersectsWith: the first shares a member with each other one) and the forAll copies.
#
# ── Stages: set:difference and containers decided later ("volatile") ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Union, intersection and the filters are monotone and computed here. Difference needs "m is not a member of the
# subtracted containers", a negation over membership that this stage derives, so it is computed in stage B
# (tio_b_sets.rules) from the facts here:
#   ?l tmf:diffFirst ?A . ?m tmf:excludedFrom ?l   # first container; members of any subtracted container
#   ?l tmf:diffUnsound tmf:Yes                     # a subtracted container is volatile: the difference has no members
# A container is volatile (`?c tmf:volatile tmf:Yes`) when its members can still grow after stage A:
#   * the icm:target of an expectation with icm:chooseFrom or icm:deliveryType: Task 15 adds the choice as
#     `?target rdfs:member ?r` in stage B (TR290 §2.5.3);
#   * the subject of set:difference (members derived in stage B);
#   * a container with "unknown membership" (`tmf:unknownMembers`): it carries a container function that is not
#     implemented (set:typesOfMembers, set:newestMember, icm:valuesOfTargetProperty, ...); its members never become
#     complete, it keeps `?c tmf:setFailure "function not implemented: ..."`;
#   * a set node with a volatile argument container (union/intersection/difference item, or the container
#     argument of resourcesWithPropertyObject); its list gets `?l tmf:volatileList tmf:Yes`. Unknown membership
#     propagates the same way.
# Stage A computes what it can for a volatile node (e.g. nothing, for a filter by a target that has no members yet);
# tio_b_sets.rules repeats the monotone rules, guarded by tmf:volatile/tmf:volatileList, so a member derived in stage B
# (a choice, or a difference result) propagates: chosen svA ⇒ SelectedSVLAN rdfs:member svA (Task 15, stage B) ⇒
# lifted to tmf:memberOf ⇒ the C-tag filter `( pon:fromSVLAN SelectedSVLAN )` matches the C-tags of svA ⇒ the
# intersection pool. Within one stage a member derived by any earlier rule propagates the same way (RETE).
# What must NOT happen is a negation over a volatile container's membership in stage B: it is incomplete there.
# So every consumer fails closed: difference does not subtract a volatile container, nor take an unknown one as its
# first argument (tmf:diffUnsound: no members, `?s tmf:setFailure`); a boolean set function with a volatile container
# argument is false here ("container membership is not final ..."); so is log:matchAll/Any/None/One over one
# (tio_a_logic cmatchNotFinal). A literal where a container is expected is "missing operand nodes". Task 15 must apply the same
# rule to icm:chooseFrom over a volatile pool (the C-tag pool): a stage-B negation over its members is unsound;
# it needs its own stratum (e.g. a further stage per choice level), not this one.
#
# ── Container argument of set:resourcesWithPropertyObject (DEVIATIONS.md entry 2, design §9.2) ─────────────────
# An object argument that is a set node (it has a set constructor) or an icm:Target stands for its members, as in the
# Java engine (isContainerArg); any other argument, a literal or a plain container included, is an object.
#
# Accepted extra form (DEVIATIONS.md entry 5, D4): `set:resourcesOfType ex:C` (one class, not a list).
#
# Negation in this file: noValue only over input facts (rdf:first of input list nodes; rdf:type icm:Target and set
# function properties of an argument, which no rule derives), as the header of tio_a_quantity requires. The forAll
# copies (builtin forAllCopy) add all triples of a copy in one rule firing, so these tests never see a partial copy.
#
# Needs the builtins of JenaBuiltins.register(): forAllCopy. Uses Jena's makeSkolem for the literal proxies.

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix fun:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/FunctionOntology/> .
@prefix icm:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentCommonModel/> .
@prefix set:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/SetOperators/> .
@prefix tmf:  <http://tmforum.org/api/v5/> .

# ── 1. Set nodes and containers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[setNodeOfType:     (?s set:resourcesOfType ?a)             -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeWithProp:   (?s set:resourcesWithProperty ?a)       -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeWithObject: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?a) -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeValues:     (?s set:valuesOfObjectProperty ?a)      -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeUnion:      (?s set:union ?a)                       -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeInter:      (?s set:intersection ?a)                -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeDiff:       (?s set:difference ?a)                  -> (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)]
[setNodeContainer:  (?s tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)                -> (?s tmf:container tmf:Yes)]
[poolContainer:     (?e icm:chooseFrom ?p) notLiteral(?p)   -> (?p tmf:container tmf:Yes)]

# A container's own members (TR292F §2: rdfs:member; the PDF's examples add explicit members to a set node too).
[liftMember: (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes) (?c rdfs:member ?m) notLiteral(?m) -> (?m tmf:memberOf ?c)]
[liftLiteral: (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes) (?c rdfs:member ?v) isLiteral(?v) makeSkolem(?n, tmf:LiteralMember, ?v)
    -> (?n tmf:proxyOf ?v) (?n tmf:memberOf ?c)]

# Lists whose items are containers: cells (the head is its own first cell).
[containerListHead: (?l tmf:containerList tmf:Yes) (?l rdf:first ?x) -> (?l tmf:cellOf ?l)]
[containerListNext: (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:cellOf ?l)]
[containerListItem: (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) notLiteral(?x) -> (?x tmf:container tmf:Yes)]

# Members in every container from this cell to the end of the list (intersection, elementOf, includedIn).
[inAllLast: (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?l tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes) (?c rdf:rest rdf:nil) (?c rdf:first ?x)
    (?m tmf:memberOf ?x) -> (?m tmf:inAllFrom ?c)]
[inAllNext: (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?l tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?m tmf:inAllFrom ?r)
    (?c rdf:first ?x) (?m tmf:memberOf ?x) -> (?m tmf:inAllFrom ?c)]

# ── 2. Volatile containers (see the header) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[volatileChoiceTarget:   (?e icm:chooseFrom ?p) (?e icm:target ?t) notLiteral(?t) -> (?t tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)]
[volatileDeliveryTarget: (?e icm:deliveryType ?d) (?e icm:target ?t) notLiteral(?t) -> (?t tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)]
[volatileDifference:     (?s set:difference ?l) -> (?s tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)]
[volatileCombined: (?l tmf:combinerOf ?s) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) (?x tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)
    -> (?s tmf:volatile tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:volatileList tmf:Yes)]
[volatileFiltered: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?x) (?x tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)
    -> (?s tmf:volatile tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:volatileList tmf:Yes)]

# Unknown membership: a container that also carries a container function no rule implements (set:typesOfMembers,
# set:newestMember, icm:valuesOfTargetProperty, ...). Its members are incomplete for good, so it is treated as
# volatile (every consumer fails closed) and the reason is kept as `?c tmf:setFailure "..."` for a later report.
# Recognised: any fun:Function (ontology) not on the implemented list; without the ontology, any set: property and
# any icm:valuesOf* or icm:intentElements property that is not implemented (the container functions of TR290).
[unknownDeclared: (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes) (?c ?f ?a) (?f rdf:type fun:Function) noValue(?f tmf:implemented tmf:Yes)
    strConcat(?f, ?iri) regex(?iri, '(?:.*[/#])?([^/#]*)', ?n) strConcat('function not implemented: ', ?n, ?t)
    -> (?c tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes) (?c tmf:setFailure ?t)]
[unknownSetFunction: (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes) (?c ?f ?a) strConcat(?f, ?iri)
    regex(?iri, 'http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/SetOperators/([^/#]+)', ?n)
    noValue(?f tmf:implemented tmf:Yes) strConcat('function not implemented: ', ?n, ?t)
    -> (?c tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes) (?c tmf:setFailure ?t)]
[unknownIcmValues: (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes) (?c ?f ?a) strConcat(?f, ?iri)
    regex(?iri, 'http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentCommonModel/(valuesOf[^/#]*|intentElements)', ?n)
    noValue(?f tmf:implemented tmf:Yes) strConcat('function not implemented: ', ?n, ?t)
    -> (?c tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes) (?c tmf:setFailure ?t)]
[unknownIsVolatile: (?c tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes) -> (?c tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)]
[unknownCombined: (?l tmf:combinerOf ?s) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) (?x tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes)
    -> (?s tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes)]
[unknownFiltered: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?x) (?x tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes)
    -> (?s tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes)]

# ── 3. set:resourcesOfType ( class ... ) (TR292F §4, §8.15): instances of the classes or their subclasses ───────

[typeListHead: (?s set:resourcesOfType ?l) (?l rdf:first ?x) -> (?l tmf:typeCellOf ?s)]
[typeListNext: (?c tmf:typeCellOf ?s) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:typeCellOf ?s)]
[typeClass: (?c tmf:typeCellOf ?s) (?c rdf:first ?k) notLiteral(?k) -> (?s tmf:typeClass ?k)]
# D4: a single class instead of a list
[typeClassShort: (?s set:resourcesOfType ?k) notLiteral(?k) notEqual(?k, rdf:nil) noValue(?k rdf:first)
    -> (?s tmf:typeClass ?k)]
[typeSubclass: (?s tmf:typeClass ?k) (?d rdfs:subClassOf ?k) -> (?s tmf:typeClass ?d)]
[typeMember: (?s tmf:typeClass ?k) (?x rdf:type ?k) -> (?x tmf:memberOf ?s)]

# ── 4. set:resourcesWithProperty ( property ... ) (§4, §8.16): subjects of any of the properties ───────────────

[withPropListHead: (?s set:resourcesWithProperty ?l) (?l rdf:first ?x) -> (?l tmf:withPropCellOf ?s)]
[withPropListNext: (?c tmf:withPropCellOf ?s) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:withPropCellOf ?s)]
[withProp: (?c tmf:withPropCellOf ?s) (?c rdf:first ?p) notLiteral(?p) notBNode(?p) -> (?s tmf:withProperty ?p)]
[withPropMember: (?s tmf:withProperty ?p) (?x ?p ?o) -> (?x tmf:memberOf ?s)]

# ── 5. set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ( property object ... ) (§4, §8.17) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Members: subjects to which the property assigns any of the objects. The property and objects are keyed by the
# argument list, so two filters on one node stay separate (and are then a union, entry 1).

[rwpoProp: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l rdf:first ?p) notLiteral(?p) notBNode(?p)
    -> (?l tmf:rwpoProp ?p)]
[rwpoCellHead: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l)]
[rwpoCellNext: (?c tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l)]

# A set node or an icm:Target argument is a container (entry 2); anything else is an object.
[rwpoContainerSet: (?c tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o) (?o tmf:setNode tmf:Yes)
    -> (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?o) (?o tmf:container tmf:Yes)]
[rwpoContainerTarget: (?c tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o) (?o rdf:type icm:Target)
    -> (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?o) (?o tmf:container tmf:Yes)]
[rwpoObjectLiteral: (?c tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o) isLiteral(?o) -> (?l tmf:rwpoObject ?o)]
[rwpoObject: (?c tmf:rwpoCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o) notLiteral(?o) noValue(?o rdf:type icm:Target)
    noValue(?o set:resourcesOfType) noValue(?o set:resourcesWithProperty) noValue(?o set:resourcesWithPropertyObject)
    noValue(?o set:valuesOfObjectProperty) noValue(?o set:union) noValue(?o set:intersection)
    noValue(?o set:difference)
    -> (?l tmf:rwpoObject ?o)]

[rwpoMatchObject: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l tmf:rwpoProp ?p) (?l tmf:rwpoObject ?o) (?x ?p ?o)
    -> (?x tmf:memberOf ?s)]
[rwpoMatchContainer: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l tmf:rwpoProp ?p) (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?c)
    (?m tmf:memberOf ?c) (?x ?p ?m) -> (?x tmf:memberOf ?s)]
[rwpoMatchContainerLiteral: (?s set:resourcesWithPropertyObject ?l) (?l tmf:rwpoProp ?p) (?l tmf:rwpoContainer ?c)
    (?n tmf:memberOf ?c) (?n tmf:proxyOf ?v) (?x ?p ?v) -> (?x tmf:memberOf ?s)]

# ── 6. set:valuesOfObjectProperty ( property object ... ) (§4, §8.20): values of the property on the objects ────

[valuesProp: (?s set:valuesOfObjectProperty ?l) (?l rdf:first ?p) notLiteral(?p) notBNode(?p)
    -> (?l tmf:valuesProp ?p)]
[valuesCellHead: (?s set:valuesOfObjectProperty ?l) (?l rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:valuesCellOf ?l)]
[valuesCellNext: (?c tmf:valuesCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?x) -> (?r tmf:valuesCellOf ?l)]
[valuesMember: (?s set:valuesOfObjectProperty ?l) (?l tmf:valuesProp ?p) (?c tmf:valuesCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o)
    notLiteral(?o) (?o ?p ?v) notLiteral(?v) -> (?v tmf:memberOf ?s)]
[valuesLiteral: (?s set:valuesOfObjectProperty ?l) (?l tmf:valuesProp ?p) (?c tmf:valuesCellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?o)
    notLiteral(?o) (?o ?p ?v) isLiteral(?v) makeSkolem(?n, tmf:LiteralMember, ?v)
    -> (?n tmf:proxyOf ?v) (?n tmf:memberOf ?s)]

# ── 7. set:union / set:intersection ( container ... ) (§3, §8.6, §8.19); empty list: no members ─────────────────

[unionList: (?s set:union ?l) notLiteral(?l) -> (?l tmf:containerList tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:combinerOf ?s)]
[unionMember: (?s set:union ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) (?m tmf:memberOf ?x) -> (?m tmf:memberOf ?s)]

[interList: (?s set:intersection ?l) notLiteral(?l)
    -> (?l tmf:containerList tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:combinerOf ?s)]
[interMember: (?s set:intersection ?l) (?m tmf:inAllFrom ?l) -> (?m tmf:memberOf ?s)]

# ── 8. set:difference ( container ... ) (§3, §8.1): the facts stage B subtracts with ───────────────────────────

[diffList: (?s set:difference ?l) notLiteral(?l) -> (?l tmf:containerList tmf:Yes) (?l tmf:combinerOf ?s)]
[diffFirst: (?s set:difference ?l) (?l rdf:first ?a) -> (?l tmf:diffFirst ?a)]
[diffExcluded: (?s set:difference ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) notEqual(?c, ?l) (?c rdf:first ?b) (?m tmf:memberOf ?b)
    -> (?m tmf:excludedFrom ?l)]
[diffUnsound: (?s set:difference ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) notEqual(?c, ?l) (?c rdf:first ?b) (?b tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)
    -> (?l tmf:diffUnsound tmf:Yes)]
# A first container whose membership is unknown can never be complete either.
[diffUnknownFirst: (?s set:difference ?l) (?l tmf:diffFirst ?a) (?a tmf:unknownMembers tmf:Yes)
    -> (?l tmf:diffUnsound tmf:Yes)]
# No members, and a reason a chooseFrom over it (Task 15) can report.
[diffUnsoundFailure: (?s set:difference ?l) (?l tmf:diffUnsound tmf:Yes)
    -> (?s tmf:setFailure "set:difference over a container whose membership is not final: no members")]

# ── 9. Boolean set functions (§5): applications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[setApplyIsMember: (?s set:isMember ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:isMember, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:isMember) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyElementOf: (?s set:elementOf ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:elementOf, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:elementOf) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyEmpty: (?s set:empty ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:empty, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:empty) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyIncludedIn: (?s set:includedIn ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:includedIn, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:includedIn) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyIntersectsWith: (?s set:intersectsWith ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:intersectsWith, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:intersectsWith) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyIdentical: (?s set:identical ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:identical, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:identical) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate)]
[setApplyForAll: (?s set:forAll ?l) makeSkolem(?k, ?s, set:forAll, ?l)
    -> (?s tmf:contribution ?k) (?k tmf:function set:forAll) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
       (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate)]

# Minimum arity (§8.2-8.5, §8.7, §8.8; identical: none given), which arguments are containers, and which need the
# all-containers walk.
[setSignatures: -> (set:isMember tmf:minArity 2) (set:elementOf tmf:minArity 2) (set:empty tmf:minArity 1)
                   (set:includedIn tmf:minArity 2) (set:intersectsWith tmf:minArity 2) (set:identical tmf:minArity 0)
                   (set:forAll tmf:minArity 3)
                   (set:isMember tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes) (set:elementOf tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes)
                   (set:empty tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes) (set:includedIn tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes)
                   (set:intersectsWith tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes) (set:identical tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes)
                   (set:elementOf tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes) (set:includedIn tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes)]

[setArgsList: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) notLiteral(?l)
    -> (?l tmf:containerList tmf:Yes)]
[setArgsNeedAll: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes)
    (?k tmf:arguments ?l) notLiteral(?l) -> (?l tmf:needsAll tmf:Yes)]
[setContainerArgAll: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes)
    (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) notLiteral(?x) -> (?k tmf:containerArg ?x)]
[setContainerArgRest: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes)
    (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) notEqual(?c, ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) notLiteral(?x)
    -> (?k tmf:containerArg ?x)]

# Decided here: not a list, too few arguments, a container whose membership is not final.
[setArgsLiteral: (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) isLiteral(?l)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[setArgsNotList: (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) notLiteral(?l) notEqual(?l, rdf:nil)
    noValue(?l rdf:first)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[setArity: (?k rdf:type tmf:SetPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:minArity ?min) (?k tmf:arguments ?l)
    listLength(?l, ?n) lessThan(?n, ?min)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
# A literal where a container is expected (§8: argument type rdfs:Container) is an error, not an empty container.
[setLiteralContainer: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:allArgsContainers tmf:Yes)
    (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) isLiteral(?x)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[setLiteralContainerRest: (?k rdf:type tmf:ContainerPredicate) (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes)
    (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l) notEqual(?c, ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) isLiteral(?x)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[forAllLiteralContainer: (?k tmf:forAllContainer ?c) isLiteral(?c)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "missing operand nodes") (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[setNotFinal: (?k tmf:containerArg ?x) (?x tmf:volatile tmf:Yes)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean)
       (?k tmf:failure "container membership is not final: it depends on a choice, on set:difference or on a function that is not implemented")
       (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]

# ── 10. Boolean set functions: positive facts for stage B ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The element tested by isMember / elementOf: the first argument, or the proxy of a literal.
[setElement: (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?l rdf:first ?x)
    notLiteral(?x) -> (?k tmf:element ?x)]
[setElementLiteral: (?k tmf:function ?f) (?f tmf:firstArgElement tmf:Yes) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?l rdf:first ?x)
    isLiteral(?x) makeSkolem(?n, tmf:LiteralMember, ?x) -> (?k tmf:element ?n)]
# isMember ( x C ... ): x is a member of any container (§8.8)
[isMemberHit: (?k tmf:function set:isMember) (?k tmf:element ?x) (?k tmf:containerArg ?c) (?x tmf:memberOf ?c)
    -> (?k tmf:setHit tmf:Yes)]
# elementOf ( x C ... ): x is a member of all containers (§8.2)
[elementOfHit: (?k tmf:function set:elementOf) (?k tmf:element ?x) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?l rdf:rest ?r)
    (?x tmf:inAllFrom ?r) -> (?k tmf:setHit tmf:Yes)]
# empty ( C ... ): true if none has members (§8.3); the hit is "some container has a member"
[emptyHit: (?k tmf:function set:empty) (?k tmf:containerArg ?c) (?m tmf:memberOf ?c) -> (?k tmf:setHit tmf:Yes)]
# intersectsWith ( C1 C2 ... ): C1 has a member in common with each of the others (§5 example: "It does not matter
# that ex:UserGroup2 and ex:UserGroup3 do not have common members, because the function only checks for the first
# argument against all other arguments"; §8.7's "members in all other containers" read with that example)
[intersectsPair: (?k tmf:function set:intersectsWith) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?l rdf:first ?c1) (?c tmf:cellOf ?l)
    notEqual(?c, ?l) (?c rdf:first ?x) (?m tmf:memberOf ?c1) (?m tmf:memberOf ?x) -> (?c tmf:sharesWithFirst ?k)]
[intersectsLast: (?c tmf:sharesWithFirst ?k) (?c rdf:rest rdf:nil) -> (?c tmf:sharesFrom ?k)]
[intersectsNext: (?c tmf:sharesWithFirst ?k) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r tmf:sharesFrom ?k) -> (?c tmf:sharesFrom ?k)]
[intersectsHit: (?k tmf:function set:intersectsWith) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) (?l rdf:rest ?r) (?r tmf:sharesFrom ?k)
    -> (?k tmf:setHit tmf:Yes)]

# forAll ( X C Q ... ) (§5, §8.4): Q (and every further argument) is evaluated once per member of C, with X replaced
# by the member. Each copy is made by forAllCopy from the input template; the copies are evaluated by the ordinary
# rules (they are new nodes with the same functions). A condition argument without any function cannot be evaluated
# (stage B: false).
[forAllArgs: (?k tmf:function set:forAll) (?k tmf:arguments ?l) listLength(?l, ?n) ge(?n, 3)
    listEntry(?l, 0, ?x) listEntry(?l, 1, ?c) (?l rdf:rest ?r1) (?r1 rdf:rest ?r2)
    -> (?k tmf:forAllVar ?x) (?k tmf:forAllContainer ?c) (?k tmf:forAllBodies ?r2)]
[forAllContainer: (?k tmf:forAllContainer ?c) notLiteral(?c) -> (?k tmf:containerArg ?c) (?c tmf:container tmf:Yes)]
[forAllBodyHead: (?k tmf:forAllBodies ?b) -> (?b tmf:bodyCellOf ?k)]
[forAllBodyNext: (?c tmf:bodyCellOf ?k) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r rdf:first ?q) -> (?r tmf:bodyCellOf ?k)]
[forAllBodyLast: (?c tmf:bodyCellOf ?k) (?c rdf:rest rdf:nil) (?c rdf:first ?q) (?q tmf:contribution ?z)
    -> (?c tmf:bodyOK tmf:Yes)]
[forAllBodyRest: (?c tmf:bodyCellOf ?k) (?c rdf:rest ?r) (?r tmf:bodyOK tmf:Yes) (?c rdf:first ?q)
    (?q tmf:contribution ?z) -> (?c tmf:bodyOK tmf:Yes)]
# The condition templates: nodes reachable from a condition argument through blank nodes (the part forAllCopy
# copies), following input properties only (not the tmf: helper facts). A template is not reported on its own
# (ContractExtractor skips tmf:forAllTemplate). A set:forAll inside a template is not supported: the inner copy would
# need the outer copy, which exists only as a stage-A deduction; fail closed.
[forAllTemplateRoot: (?c tmf:bodyCellOf ?k) (?c rdf:first ?q) notLiteral(?q)
    -> (?q tmf:inTemplateOf ?k) (?q tmf:forAllTemplate tmf:Yes)]
[forAllTemplateNext: (?n tmf:inTemplateOf ?k) (?n ?p ?o) isBNode(?o) strConcat(?p, ?ps)
    regex(?ps, '(?!http://tmforum.org/api/v5/).*') -> (?o tmf:inTemplateOf ?k)]
[forAllNested: (?n tmf:inTemplateOf ?k) (?n set:forAll ?l)
    -> (?k rdf:value "false"^^xsd:boolean) (?k tmf:failure "set:forAll nested in set:forAll is not supported")
       (?k tmf:valuedInA tmf:Yes)]
[forAllHasMember: (?k tmf:forAllContainer ?s) (?m tmf:memberOf ?s) -> (?k tmf:forAllHasMember tmf:Yes)]
[forAllCopy: (?c tmf:bodyCellOf ?k) (?c rdf:first ?q) notLiteral(?q) (?k tmf:forAllVar ?x)
    (?k tmf:forAllContainer ?s) (?m tmf:memberOf ?s)
    -> forAllCopy(?k, ?q, ?x, ?m)]
